WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.128
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.128 --> 00:00:02.507
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.507 --> 00:00:04.273
My one word is "believe" and I believe

00:00:04.273 --> 00:00:05.826
that entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:05.826 --> 00:00:07.495
of the major problems in the world.

00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:10.807
So today's message is be decisive.

00:00:10.807 --> 00:00:12.233
Over to you, Anna Wintour.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:14.416
(Rooster crowing)

00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:17.266
- ♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.266 --> 00:00:20.174
- ♫ Espresso, keep me going

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:23.761
- ♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.761 --> 00:00:25.300
- I try and be decisive.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.559
I try, even if I don't know
what the hell I'm doing,

00:00:27.559 --> 00:00:32.550
I try to be decisive because
I think it's very comforting

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.391
and reassuring, and important

00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:36.377
to the people that work with you

00:00:36.377 --> 00:00:38.945
to feel that whoever is in charge

00:00:38.945 --> 00:00:41.346
knows what they're doing, and
knows what they're thinking,

00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:42.704
and that if it's a yes, it's a yes,

00:00:42.704 --> 00:00:43.537
and it's a no, it's a no.

00:00:43.537 --> 00:00:46.500
I mean, I don't think of myself as a boss.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.959
I mean, I think of myself as
someone who's giving direction,

00:00:49.959 --> 00:00:53.449
guidance, and vice versa (people talking).

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:55.121
- So I don't know if I
agree about the advice

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.699
of trying to be decisive

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.670
even if you don't know what you're doing,

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.377
but I do agree with the fact that

00:01:00.377 --> 00:01:02.208
people want to work for a leader

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:03.416
who knows what they're up to,

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:04.666
what they're trying to accomplish,

00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:06.602
if there's a clear mission, a clear path.

00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:09.792
Nobody wants to work for a
leader who's all over the place.

00:01:09.792 --> 00:01:12.351
Who says one thing on day,
one thing another day.

00:01:12.351 --> 00:01:13.742
Nobody wants to work for that person,

00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:16.663
so if you are an entrepreneur
and you're building up a team

00:01:16.663 --> 00:01:17.931
then you have to be really careful

00:01:17.931 --> 00:01:19.393
about the direction that you give them

00:01:19.393 --> 00:01:21.419
and have confidence in the
direction that you're going.

00:01:21.419 --> 00:01:23.667
The way that I do it I
think works pretty well,

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:27.085
at least for me, is one, being
really clear on the mission.

00:01:27.085 --> 00:01:28.299
Like, here's what we're trying to do.

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:29.968
Here's what I'm trying to accomplish.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.118
This is going to happen.

00:01:31.118 --> 00:01:33.949
We are going to make
this big thing happen,

00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:36.639
but the specifics of how
to get there may change.

00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:39.962
Not every project will
work out, and that's okay.

00:01:39.962 --> 00:01:42.320
You're going to have little
bumps, and bruises, and failures

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.309
along the way, lots of them.

00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:46.033
Lots of little bumps, and
bruises, and failures,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.410
and hopefully you keep the size of them,

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.912
you know, how big the
impact is to a minimum,

00:01:50.912 --> 00:01:52.220
but you're trying out lots of them

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.800
because you need to go through that pain

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.195
to get to the success.

00:01:55.195 --> 00:01:57.383
But even though those little
things didn't work out,

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:01.437
you're decisive, and clear,
and understand the big picture

00:02:01.437 --> 00:02:03.796
of where you're going and
you believe it in your heart

00:02:03.796 --> 00:02:05.294
that it's going to happen.

00:02:05.294 --> 00:02:08.205
If the leader does not have
confidence in what's happening

00:02:08.205 --> 00:02:10.432
nobody underneath you is going
to have confidence either.

00:02:10.432 --> 00:02:13.490
If you are at all concerned that
this is not going to work out,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.100
you can bet that that's
going to spread like wildfire

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.070
all the way down the organization.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.653
You need to believe hardest,
believe most of anybody

00:02:21.653 --> 00:02:23.900
in your company that this
big thing that you're trying

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.030
to accomplish is possible.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.359
Again, the how to
accomplish it will change.

00:02:28.359 --> 00:02:30.059
You don't need to know the specifics,

00:02:30.059 --> 00:02:32.773
but you have to have that point,

00:02:32.773 --> 00:02:34.961
The guiding light, the destination.

00:02:34.961 --> 00:02:36.657
Here's what we are trying to accomplish.

00:02:36.657 --> 00:02:38.081
Here's the war we are trying to fight,

00:02:38.081 --> 00:02:39.959
and it's 100% winnable.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.238
That confidence will inspire
people to follow you,

00:02:43.238 --> 00:02:46.715
and will encourage them to
push beyond their comfort zone,

00:02:46.715 --> 00:02:50.001
bring more creativity,
bring more of themselves

00:02:50.001 --> 00:02:52.679
because they believe in what you believe.

00:02:52.679 --> 00:02:54.741
So the question today is I'm curious,

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.380
what is the big thing that
you are trying to accomplish

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.960
that you believe in
your heart is possible,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.200
even though others around you

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.730
might think it's a little crazy.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.332
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:03:04.332 --> 00:03:05.601
I'm super curious to find out.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.677
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Jennifer Stier.

00:03:07.677 --> 00:03:09.643
Jennifer, thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:03:09.643 --> 00:03:11.283
of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:13.091
It really, really means a lot to me,

00:03:13.091 --> 00:03:14.713
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:14.713 --> 00:03:16.123
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:16.123 --> 00:03:17.163
I believe in you.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.068
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:03:19.068 --> 00:03:21.229
and whatever your one word is,

00:03:21.229 --> 00:03:22.739
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:25.279
for another shot of entspresso.

00:03:25.279 --> 00:03:28.100
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.620
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.201
(typing noise)

00:03:34.201 --> 00:03:37.031
- Decision making is a process, right?

00:03:37.031 --> 00:03:38.963
The question is, what
filters are you using

00:03:38.963 --> 00:03:40.011
to make decisions?

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:42.783
Are you making decisions based
on the financial rewards?

00:03:42.783 --> 00:03:45.481
Are you making decisions based
on how easy the work will be?

00:03:45.481 --> 00:03:47.442
I mean, I remember in college, you know,

00:03:47.442 --> 00:03:49.787
they would give you this book
where all the students would

00:03:49.787 --> 00:03:52.006
rate the classes, and they
would rate things like

00:03:52.006 --> 00:03:55.509
how easy the class was,
and how much they liked

00:03:55.509 --> 00:03:56.488
the professor.

00:03:56.488 --> 00:03:59.459
And, you know, the first
year I picked all my classes

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:03.191
based on workload, and I picked
everything a low workload,

00:04:03.191 --> 00:04:05.441
you know, and pretty bored.

00:04:06.316 --> 00:04:09.399
Didn't work very hard which was fine,

00:04:10.246 --> 00:04:12.791
nothing was dynamic and
nothing really excited me.

00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:14.494
And I, thank goodness, learned that.

00:04:14.494 --> 00:04:16.564
And so, the second year,
I picked all my classes

00:04:16.564 --> 00:04:20.134
by professor rating,
regardless of the workload.

00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:22.427
So, every class I had I
had these dynamic, amazing,

00:04:22.427 --> 00:04:25.245
incredible human beings
passing on their knowledge,

00:04:25.245 --> 00:04:28.782
and you were excited to work
hard for them, you know?

00:04:28.782 --> 00:04:30.783
And so, again, the question is

00:04:30.783 --> 00:04:32.243
what are the filters we're using,

00:04:32.243 --> 00:04:34.669
and so, if you're only
chasing the mighty dollar,

00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:36.377
then you will have jobs that'll pay you

00:04:36.377 --> 00:04:37.737
a little more than they'll ask,

00:04:37.737 --> 00:04:39.268
but are you enjoying yourself?

00:04:39.268 --> 00:04:41.877
And I talked to a guy
recently who is in bad shape.

00:04:41.877 --> 00:04:45.146
Like, he really hates his
life and he's really depressed

00:04:45.146 --> 00:04:46.478
and he doesn't know what to do.

00:04:46.478 --> 00:04:48.418
And so we were going through
all his old jobs, you know,

00:04:48.418 --> 00:04:49.969
and I said, "Give me a
job that you've loved,"

00:04:49.969 --> 00:04:50.898
and he hadn't.

00:04:50.898 --> 00:04:53.089
Every single job he's
chosen out of college

00:04:53.089 --> 00:04:55.828
he picked because of the money,
and if something offered him

00:04:55.828 --> 00:05:00.378
more somewhere else, he took
it, you know, regardless.

00:05:00.378 --> 00:05:02.174
And the amazing thing is he plateaued

00:05:02.174 --> 00:05:04.865
because if you're only chasing the result,

00:05:04.865 --> 00:05:08.319
if you're only chasing the
thing that makes it easy, right,

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:10.852
then eventually you will get bored,

00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.807
or they'll get bored of you, right,

00:05:12.807 --> 00:05:13.767
and you plateau.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.706
In other words, chasing
the almighty dollar,

00:05:15.706 --> 00:05:17.453
if that's your only thing,
it eventually flattens out.

00:05:17.453 --> 00:05:18.286
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:05:18.286 --> 00:05:20.260
Whereas if you're chasing
the thing that excites you:

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.437
the human beings to be around,
the work that excites you,

00:05:22.437 --> 00:05:27.078
the stuff that, you know,
you can get passionate about,

00:05:27.078 --> 00:05:28.320
you know?

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.090
The irony is you'll actually
make way, way more, right?

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.308
Because you're excited and they
appreciate your excitement,

00:05:34.308 --> 00:05:35.169
and they reward your excitement,

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:37.658
and you're better at your work
because you want to work harder

00:05:37.658 --> 00:05:38.767
at all of that stuff.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.677
You don't have to strain to work harder.

00:05:41.677 --> 00:05:44.999
So, decision making is simply
a matter of filters, you know?

00:05:44.999 --> 00:05:46.729
And so, I've made decisions in my life

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:48.381
that I would rather be happy than right.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.131
I'd rather do good than get rich,

00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:56.381
and so the decisions I
make put me in positions

00:05:56.381 --> 00:05:58.016
where when I leave any engagement,

00:05:58.016 --> 00:05:59.690
when I leave any meeting I feel

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.693
that I've contributed, right?

00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:05.220
Rare are the times anymore
where you walk around going,

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.930
"Just think of the money.
Just think of the money,

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.759
think of the money," you know,

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:10.280
because it doesn't feel nice.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.380
And experience I have, I
don't enjoy travailing to them

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.148
and I don't enjoy traveling home.

00:06:15.148 --> 00:06:15.981
Where, if I have an amazing experience,

00:06:15.981 --> 00:06:17.235
I am looking forward to getting there

00:06:17.235 --> 00:06:18.483
and I'm excited when I leave.

00:06:18.483 --> 00:06:19.603
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:06:19.603 --> 00:06:21.652
You know, so it's just decision ma..

00:06:21.652 --> 00:06:23.714
Decision making is just a
matter of what filters you use,

00:06:23.714 --> 00:06:27.929
and if you're good about keeping
those filters up and clear,

00:06:27.929 --> 00:06:29.185
then make your decision.

00:06:29.185 --> 00:06:32.256
I don't judge anybody by if they choose

00:06:32.256 --> 00:06:33.723
to use different filters.

00:06:33.723 --> 00:06:35.805
These are just the filters I choose

00:06:35.805 --> 00:06:37.752
to live my life, you know?

00:06:37.752 --> 00:06:40.492
Not right or wrong, just
those are my decisions.

00:06:40.492 --> 00:06:41.721
You know, that's my filter.

00:06:41.721 --> 00:06:42.554
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:06:42.554 --> 00:06:44.108
- That is something I learned in Asia

00:06:44.108 --> 00:06:46.349
because, obviously, when you
take a CEO job in a company,

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:48.060
you learn a lot, you learn a lot.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.252
One other thing I learned,
particularly, in Japan,

00:06:50.252 --> 00:06:53.017
That from time to time,
making quick decision

00:06:53.017 --> 00:06:55.841
is going to hurt the
execution of the decision

00:06:55.841 --> 00:06:56.833
because what do you want?

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:58.394
When you make a decision,
what do you want?

00:06:58.394 --> 00:07:00.873
You want to transform reality.

00:07:00.873 --> 00:07:01.893
You don't want to make a decision

00:07:01.893 --> 00:07:03.405
for the sake of making a decision.

00:07:03.405 --> 00:07:05.482
You make a decision because
you want something to change.

00:07:05.482 --> 00:07:08.801
So, your goal is the thing changed.

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:10.370
That's your goal, so now,

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.197
the question is when should
you make the decision

00:07:13.197 --> 00:07:16.070
in order to make sure
that the thing has changed

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.912
in the fastest period of time.

00:07:18.912 --> 00:07:21.183
So, from time to time you have
to wait to make the decision

00:07:21.183 --> 00:07:24.000
because you're preparing
people to execute.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.032
From time to time you need to
make the decision very early.

00:07:27.032 --> 00:07:28.532
From time to time, a little bit late,

00:07:28.532 --> 00:07:31.430
but when I say decisiveness means capacity

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.857
to make the decision
at the appropriate time

00:07:33.857 --> 00:07:35.127
because at the end of the day,

00:07:35.127 --> 00:07:38.302
what you need is reality changes.

00:07:38.302 --> 00:07:39.449
That's your goal.

